Hooray for stupid ascension tricks! Let's get down to the brass tacks.

After reading the story of Tenaya at
http://groups.google.ca/group/rec.games.roguelike.nethack/msg/5a956e85015c2aae?
I decided I would also like to do a racial ascension, but as the Orc
had already been done, I decided to do a Dwarf.

Though it wouldn't make much difference to my tools and general items,
it will affect my weapons and armour, of which I will only be using
traditional dwarven equipment:

Weapons: Pick-axe, dwarvish mattock, dwarvish short sword, dwarvish
spear
Armour: Dwarvish mithril-coat, dwarvish cloak, dwarvish helmet, iron
shoes, dwarvish roundshield.

Obviously, I've made a *couple* of concessions; the pick-axe and iron
shoes don't have "dwarvish" in the name. But honestly, who else do you
see carrying them?

In Slash'EM, the only classes a Dwarf can be are Arc, Cav and Val. My
problem is deciding between them:

ARCHEOLOGIST
Advantages: Starts with a pick-axe, may achieve Expert in pick-axe
skill (allowing the dwarvish mattock)
Disadvantages: Kind of wimpy and relies on a combination of melee and
magic skills - but dwarvish armour is not forgiving of magic

CAVE(WO)MAN
Advantages: May achieve Expert in spear skill, built as a combat
wombat
Disadvantages: Does not start with a dwarven weapon - will force me to
fight to the mines barehanded and naked

VALKYRIE
Advantages: Starts with a dwarvish spear, built as a combat wombat
Disadvanges: May not reach expert in any dwarvish weapons

In addition, any dwarvish armour will have to be secured on-site,
which is additionally difficult because all dwarves will be peaceful -
except for perhaps cloaks, how do I get the equipment without taking
an alignment hit?

Anything else I haven't thought of? Advice? Attempts to talk me out of
such suicide?



